// The Client domain: a seam on the function that takes the client apart.

#ifndef WXL_SEAM_BEFORE
#error "define WXL_SEAM_BEFORE(domain, name, symbol, ret, conv, params) before including client.def"
#endif

// Takes the client apart: the glue, the add-ons, the client databases, the sound, the script
// context, the console, in that order. One caller, on the way out of the main function, while
// everything a mod may hold is still alive. Before announces the shutdown stage, releases what
// the mods left hooked or open, and unloads them; After does nothing.
//
// A file-level static, but with no arguments and no result: a cdecl detour is correct whatever
// convention the compiler gave it.
WXL_SEAM_BEFORE(Client, Destroy, "WowClientDestroy", void, cdecl, ())

// MSVC takes a file that expands to nothing outside its opening #ifndef X ... #endif for one
// guarded by X, and skips it when it is included again with X defined: this table is read
// several times in one translation unit, under shapes that may leave it empty. A directive
// after the rows keeps it from looking guarded.
#ifdef WXL_TABLE_END
#endif
